  user_input {
    user_response: "1 \302\267 Role & Project Identity\n\nYou are an expert frontend developer and UI/UX designer specializing in multilingual React applications and marketplace platforms.\n\nYour task is to build \"AccoNet\" (\330\243\331\203\331\210\331\206\331\212\330\252) \342\200\224 Algeria\'s first digital platform connecting accounting professionals (accountants, auditors, tax consultants) with businesses, SMEs, startups, and associations.\n\nThink of it as the \"Upwork for Algerian accounting services\" \342\200\224 a polished, production-grade frontend demo built entirely with React + Tailwind CSS, powered by realistic mock data (no backend needed).\n\nThe platform must feel local, trustworthy, and modern \342\200\224 built for Algeria, not translated from elsewhere.\n\n---\n\n2 \302\267 Tech Stack & Constraints\n\n## Tech Stack (Frontend Only)\n\n- Framework: React (functional components + hooks)\n- Styling: Tailwind CSS\n- Routing: React Router v6 (client-side only)\n- Icons: Lucide React or Heroicons\n- Fonts: Cairo or Tajawal (Google Fonts) \342\200\224 Arabic-compatible, works in all 3 languages\n- State: useState / useContext (no Redux needed)\n- NO backend, NO API calls, NO database\n- All data comes from mock JSON objects defined in the codebase\n\n## Trilingual Support (CRITICAL)\n- Languages: Arabic (AR), French (FR), English (EN)\n- Arabic is RTL \342\200\224 the entire layout must flip direction when AR is active (dir=\"rtl\")\n- A language switcher must be visible in the navbar at all times\n- All UI strings, labels, and content must be translated in all 3 languages\n- Use a central i18n object or context \342\200\224 never hardcode display strings\n\n## Responsive Design\n- Mobile-first (Android-dominant market in Algeria)\n- Breakpoints: mobile (default), md (tablet), lg (desktop)\n- Navigation collapses to a hamburger menu on mobile\n\n---\n\n3 \302\267 Mock Data Specification\n\n## Mock Data \342\200\224 define these in /src/data/mockData.js\n\n### professionals[] \342\200\224 at least 8 entries, each with:\n- id, name (AR + FR + EN), avatar initials, photo placeholder\n- specialty: one of [Chartered Accountant, Statutory Auditor, Certified Accountant, Tax Consultant, Judicial Expert]\n- wilaya: realistic Algerian cities (Alger, Oran, Constantine, Annaba, Tizi Ouzou, S\303\251tif, Blida, B\303\251ja\303\257a...)\n- rating (4.0\342\200\2235.0), reviewCount, hourlyRate (DZD), available (bool)\n- yearsExperience, bio (short paragraph in all 3 languages)\n- services[] (list of 4\342\200\2236 services they offer)\n- reviews[] (3 reviews each with client name, rating, comment, date)\n\n### clients[] \342\200\224 at least 4 entries:\n- id, companyName, sector, wilaya, logo initials\n- NIF (fake), RC (fake), activeContracts[], pendingTasks[]\n\n### contracts[] \342\200\224 at least 5 entries:\n- id, professionalId, clientId, title, status (active/completed/pending)\n- startDate, endDate, value (DZD), scope description\n\n### tasks[] \342\200\224 at least 8 entries:\n- id, contractId, title, deadline, status (todo/in-progress/done)\n- type: one of [tax-filing, audit, bookkeeping, advisory, declaration]\n\n### testimonials[] \342\200\224 6 entries:\n- clientName, company, wilaya, rating, comment (all 3 languages), date\n\n### wilayas[] \342\200\224 all 48 Algerian wilayas for the search filter dropdown\n\n---\n\n4 \302\267 Pages & Screens\n\n## Pages to Build (React Router routes)\n\n### / \342\200\224 Landing Page\n- Hero section: headline, subtext, 2 CTAs (Find Accountant / Join as Pro), animated stats (professionals count, wilayas, businesses)\n- Search bar: keyword + wilaya dropdown + specialty dropdown\n- Featured professionals grid (top 4 cards)\n- \"How it works\" section \342\200\224 4 steps with icons\n- AI Tools section \342\200\224 6 feature cards\n- Testimonials carousel/grid\n- Footer with logo, tagline, links\n\n### /search \342\200\224 Search & Discovery Page\n- Sidebar filters: wilaya, specialty, availability, min rating, price range\n- Results grid of professional cards\n- Each card: avatar, name, specialty, wilaya, rating, price, availability badge, \"View Profile\" button\n- Sort by: rating, price, experience\n- Filter count badge, reset filters button\n\n### /professional/:id \342\200\224 Professional Profile Page\n- Header: large avatar, name, specialty badge, wilaya, rating, availability, hire button\n- Tabs: About | Services | Reviews | Experience\n- About tab: bio, stats (years exp, clients served, completion rate)\n- Services tab: list of services with description\n- Reviews tab: list of client reviews with stars and date\n- Experience tab: timeline of professional history\n- Sticky sidebar on desktop: rate, availability, \"Hire Now\" + \"Send Message\" buttons\n\n### /dashboard/client \342\200\224 Client Dashboard\n- Welcome header with company name\n- Stats row: active tasks, active contracts, pending documents, unread messages\n- Upcoming deadlines list (with urgency color coding)\n- Active contracts list with professional avatar, status badge, progress bar\n- Recent activity feed\n\n### /dashboard/professional \342\200\224 Professional Dashboard\n- Welcome header with professional name + specialty\n- Stats row: active clients, pending tasks, monthly earnings, rating\n- Task inbox list (todo / in-progress / done tabs)\n- Upcoming deadlines with date and client name\n- Earnings summary card (monthly mock chart using CSS bars)\n\n### /tools \342\200\224 AI Tools Page (showcase only, simulated UI)\n- Grid of 6 tool cards, each expandable\n- Each tool shows a simulated interface (fake input/output UI to demo the concept)\n- Tools: Auto Journal Entry, OCR Parser, Tax Templates, Statement Audit, AI Analysis, Secure Exchange\n\n### /login and /register \342\200\224 Auth Pages (UI only, no real auth)\n- Clean split-screen design\n- Register page has two paths: \"I\'m a Business\" vs \"I\'m a Professional\"\n- Professional registration shows extra fields: specialty, accreditation number, wilaya\n\n---\n\n5 \302\267 Design System & Brand\n\n## AccoNet Design System\n\n### Brand Colors\n- Primary: #0F6E56 (deep teal \342\200\224 trust, professionalism)\n- Primary light: #E1F5EE\n- Primary dark: #085041\n- Accent: #F59E0B (amber \342\200\224 action, warmth)\n- Neutral: #1F2937 (dark gray for text)\n- Surface: #F9FAFB (light background)\n- White: #FFFFFF\n\n### Typography\n- Font: \"Cairo\" (Arabic + Latin, Google Fonts) \342\200\224 covers all 3 languages beautifully\n- Heading: font-weight 700, tight tracking\n- Body: font-weight 400, line-height 1.7\n- Code/numbers: font-mono for amounts (DZD)\n\n### Component Style\n- Cards: white bg, subtle shadow (shadow-sm), rounded-xl, hover:shadow-md transition\n- Buttons: primary = teal bg + white text; secondary = white bg + teal border; ghost = transparent\n- Badges: rounded-full, colored by status (green=available, amber=busy, blue=new)\n- Inputs: rounded-lg, border-gray-200, focus:border-teal, focus:ring-teal/20\n- Avatar: colored circle with initials, consistent size per context\n\n### RTL Rules (Arabic mode)\n- Set dir=\"rtl\" on  when language is AR\n- Flex row direction reverses automatically\n- Text aligns right\n- Padding/margin sides swap (use Tailwind\'s RTL utilities: rtl:pr-4, rtl:pl-0 etc.)\n- Icons that imply direction (arrows) must flip: rtl:rotate-180\n- The layout must look NATIVE in Arabic, not mirrored as an afterthought\n\n### Micro-interactions\n- Smooth page transitions (opacity fade)\n- Card hover: translateY(-2px) + shadow increase\n- Language switcher: instant re-render, no flash\n- Loading states: skeleton cards (gray animated pulse) for search results\n- Availability badge: soft pulse animation for \"Available\" status\n\n---\n\n6 \302\267 Instructions for Claude\n\n## How to work on AccoNet\n\n### When I ask you to build a page or component:\n- Write complete, working React code \342\200\224 no placeholders like \"add content here\"\n- Import and use the mock data from mockData.js\n- Include all 3 language translations inline or via the i18n context\n- Apply RTL support for Arabic correctly\n- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes only \342\200\224 no custom CSS files\n- Make it fully responsive (mobile + desktop)\n- Components should be self-contained and reusable\n\n### File structure to follow:\nsrc/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 data/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 mockData.js          \342\206\220 all mock professionals, clients, contracts, tasks\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 i18n/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 translations.js      \342\206\220 all UI strings in AR, FR, EN\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 context/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 LanguageContext.jsx  \342\206\220 language state + switcher logic\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Navbar.jsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Footer.jsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProfessionalCard.jsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SearchFilters.jsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 StatCard.jsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ...\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 pages/\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Landing.jsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Search.jsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProfessionalProfile.jsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ClientDashboard.jsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProfessionalDashboard.jsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Tools.jsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Login.jsx\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Register.jsx\n\n### Quality bar:\n- The demo must look like a real funded startup\'s product, not a tutorial project\n- Every screen must feel complete \342\200\224 no empty states unless intentional\n- Arabic mode must look like it was designed for Arabic first\n- Mock data must be realistic: real Algerian wilayas, realistic DZD rates, real accounting service names\n- When in doubt, make it more polished, not less\n\n### Respond in the same language I write to you (AR / FR / EN)\n\n"
    items {
      text: "1 \302\267 Role & Project Identity\n\nYou are an expert frontend developer and UI/UX designer specializing in multilingual React applications and marketplace platforms.\n\nYour task is to build \"AccoNet\" (\330\243\331\203\331\210\331\206\331\212\330\252) \342\200\224 Algeria\'s first digital platform connecting accounting professionals (accountants, auditors, tax consultants) with businesses, SMEs, startups, and associations.\n\nThink of it as the \"Upwork for Algerian accounting services\" \342\200\224 a polished, production-grade frontend demo built entirely with React + Tailwind CSS, powered by realistic mock data (no backend needed).\n\nThe platform must feel local, trustworthy, and modern \342\200\224 built for Algeria, not translated from elsewhere.\n\n---\n\n2 \302\267 Tech Stack & Constraints\n\n## Tech Stack (Frontend Only)\n\n- Framework: React (functional components + hooks)\n- Styling: Tailwind CSS\n- Routing: React Router v6 (client-side only)\n- Icons: Lucide React or Heroicons\n- Fonts: Cairo or Tajawal (Google Fonts) \342\200\224 Arabic-compatible, works in all 3 languages\n- State: useState / useContext (no Redux needed)\n- NO backend, NO API calls, NO database\n- All data comes from mock JSON objects defined in the codebase\n\n## Trilingual Support (CRITICAL)\n- Languages: Arabic (AR), French (FR), English (EN)\n- Arabic is RTL \342\200\224 the entire layout must flip direction when AR is active (dir=\"rtl\")\n- A language switcher must be visible in the navbar at all times\n- All UI strings, labels, and content must be translated in all 3 languages\n- Use a central i18n object or context \342\200\224 never hardcode display strings\n\n## Responsive Design\n- Mobile-first (Android-dominant market in Algeria)\n- Breakpoints: mobile (default), md (tablet), lg (desktop)\n- Navigation collapses to a hamburger menu on mobile\n\n---\n\n3 \302\267 Mock Data Specification\n\n## Mock Data \342\200\224 define these in /src/data/mockData.js\n\n### professionals[] \342\200\224 at least 8 entries, each with:\n- id, name (AR + FR + EN), avatar initials, photo placeholder\n- specialty: one of [Chartered Accountant, Statutory Auditor, Certified Accountant, Tax Consultant, Judicial Expert]\n- wilaya: realistic Algerian cities (Alger, Oran, Constantine, Annaba, Tizi Ouzou, S\303\251tif, Blida, B\303\251ja\303\257a...)\n- rating (4.0\342\200\2235.0), reviewCount, hourlyRate (DZD), available (bool)\n- yearsExperience, bio (short paragraph in all 3 languages)\n- services[] (list of 4\342\200\2236 services they offer)\n- reviews[] (3 reviews each with client name, rating, comment, date)\n\n### clients[] \342\200\224 at least 4 entries:\n- id, companyName, sector, wilaya, logo initials\n- NIF (fake), RC (fake), activeContracts[], pendingTasks[]\n\n### contracts[] \342\200\224 at least 5 entries:\n- id, professionalId, clientId, title, status (active/completed/pending)\n- startDate, endDate, value (DZD), scope description\n\n### tasks[] \342\200\224 at least 8 entries:\n- id, contractId, title, deadline, status (todo/in-progress/done)\n- type: one of [tax-filing, audit, bookkeeping, advisory, declaration]\n\n### testimonials[] \342\200\224 6 entries:\n- clientName, company, wilaya, rating, comment (all 3 languages), date\n\n### wilayas[] \342\200\224 all 48 Algerian wilayas for the search filter dropdown\n\n---\n\n4 \302\267 Pages & Screens\n\n## Pages to Build (React Router routes)\n\n### / \342\200\224 Landing Page\n- Hero section: headline, subtext, 2 CTAs (Find Accountant / Join as Pro), animated stats (professionals count, wilayas, businesses)\n- Search bar: keyword + wilaya dropdown + specialty dropdown\n- Featured professionals grid (top 4 cards)\n- \"How it works\" section \342\200\224 4 steps with icons\n- AI Tools section \342\200\224 6 feature cards\n- Testimonials carousel/grid\n- Footer with logo, tagline, links\n\n### /search \342\200\224 Search & Discovery Page\n- Sidebar filters: wilaya, specialty, availability, min rating, price range\n- Results grid of professional cards\n- Each card: avatar, name, specialty, wilaya, rating, price, availability badge, \"View Profile\" button\n- Sort by: rating, price, experience\n- Filter count badge, reset filters button\n\n### /professional/:id \342\200\224 Professional Profile Page\n- Header: large avatar, name, specialty badge, wilaya, rating, availability, hire button\n- Tabs: About | Services | Reviews | Experience\n- About tab: bio, stats (years exp, clients served, completion rate)\n- Services tab: list of services with description\n- Reviews tab: list of client reviews with stars and date\n- Experience tab: timeline of professional history\n- Sticky sidebar on desktop: rate, availability, \"Hire Now\" + \"Send Message\" buttons\n\n### /dashboard/client \342\200\224 Client Dashboard\n- Welcome header with company name\n- Stats row: active tasks, active contracts, pending documents, unread messages\n- Upcoming deadlines list (with urgency color coding)\n- Active contracts list with professional avatar, status badge, progress bar\n- Recent activity feed\n\n### /dashboard/professional \342\200\224 Professional Dashboard\n- Welcome header with professional name + specialty\n- Stats row: active clients, pending tasks, monthly earnings, rating\n- Task inbox list (todo / in-progress / done tabs)\n- Upcoming deadlines with date and client name\n- Earnings summary card (monthly mock chart using CSS bars)\n\n### /tools \342\200\224 AI Tools Page (showcase only, simulated UI)\n- Grid of 6 tool cards, each expandable\n- Each tool shows a simulated interface (fake input/output UI to demo the concept)\n- Tools: Auto Journal Entry, OCR Parser, Tax Templates, Statement Audit, AI Analysis, Secure Exchange\n\n### /login and /register \342\200\224 Auth Pages (UI only, no real auth)\n- Clean split-screen design\n- Register page has two paths: \"I\'m a Business\" vs \"I\'m a Professional\"\n- Professional registration shows extra fields: specialty, accreditation number, wilaya\n\n---\n\n5 \302\267 Design System & Brand\n\n## AccoNet Design System\n\n### Brand Colors\n- Primary: #0F6E56 (deep teal \342\200\224 trust, professionalism)\n- Primary light: #E1F5EE\n- Primary dark: #085041\n- Accent: #F59E0B (amber \342\200\224 action, warmth)\n- Neutral: #1F2937 (dark gray for text)\n- Surface: #F9FAFB (light background)\n- White: #FFFFFF\n\n### Typography\n- Font: \"Cairo\" (Arabic + Latin, Google Fonts) \342\200\224 covers all 3 languages beautifully\n- Heading: font-weight 700, tight tracking\n- Body: font-weight 400, line-height 1.7\n- Code/numbers: font-mono for amounts (DZD)\n\n### Component Style\n- Cards: white bg, subtle shadow (shadow-sm), rounded-xl, hover:shadow-md transition\n- Buttons: primary = teal bg + white text; secondary = white bg + teal border; ghost = transparent\n- Badges: rounded-full, colored by status (green=available, amber=busy, blue=new)\n- Inputs: rounded-lg, border-gray-200, focus:border-teal, focus:ring-teal/20\n- Avatar: colored circle with initials, consistent size per context\n\n### RTL Rules (Arabic mode)\n- Set dir=\"rtl\" on  when language is AR\n- Flex row direction reverses automatically\n- Text aligns right\n- Padding/margin sides swap (use Tailwind\'s RTL utilities: rtl:pr-4, rtl:pl-0 etc.)\n- Icons that imply direction (arrows) must flip: rtl:rotate-180\n- The layout must look NATIVE in Arabic, not mirrored as an afterthought\n\n### Micro-interactions\n- Smooth page transitions (opacity fade)\n- Card hover: translateY(-2px) + shadow increase\n- Language switcher: instant re-render, no flash\n- Loading states: skeleton cards (gray animated pulse) for search results\n- Availability badge: soft pulse animation for \"Available\" status\n\n---\n\n6 \302\267 Instructions for Claude\n\n## How to work on AccoNet\n\n### When I ask you to build a page or component:\n- Write complete, working React code \342\200\224 no placeholders like \"add content here\"\n- Import and use the mock data from mockData.js\n- Include all 3 language translations inline or via the i18n context\n- Apply RTL support for Arabic correctly\n- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes only \342\200\224 no custom CSS files\n- Make it fully responsive (mobile + desktop)\n- Components should be self-contained and reusable\n\n### File structure to follow:\nsrc/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 data/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 mockData.js          \342\206\220 all mock professionals, clients, contracts, tasks\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 i18n/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 translations.js      \342\206\220 all UI strings in AR, FR, EN\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 context/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 LanguageContext.jsx  \342\206\220 language state + switcher logic\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Navbar.jsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Footer.jsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProfessionalCard.jsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SearchFilters.jsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 StatCard.jsx\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ...\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 pages/\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Landing.jsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Search.jsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProfessionalProfile.jsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ClientDashboard.jsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProfessionalDashboard.jsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Tools.jsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Login.jsx\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Register.jsx\n\n### Quality bar:\n- The demo must look like a real funded startup\'s product, not a tutorial project\n- Every screen must feel complete \342\200\224 no empty states unless intentional\n- Arabic mode must look like it was designed for Arabic first\n- Mock data must be realistic: real Algerian wilayas, realistic DZD rates, real accounting service names\n- When in doubt, make it more polished, not less\n\n### Respond in the same language I write to you (AR / FR / EN)\n\n"
    }
  }
}
