    thinking: "**Assessing Fonts\' Utility**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased with the current global styling, especially the font imports: Amiri, Playfair Display, Cairo, Inter, and JetBrains Mono. These fonts give me an excellent base for a beautiful editorial design, and I\'m keen to begin exploring how they complement one another.\n\n\n**Redesigning the Landing Page**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on redesigning `Landing.tsx`. I\'ve decided on an asymmetric layout with a split-column grid, featuring the typography and CTA on one side, and a dynamic \"Accounting Ledger Core & Task Feed Preview Widget\" on the other. This interactive element aims to immediately convey the product\'s capabilities. I\'m prioritizing RTL-native design and editorial blocks with horizontal rhythm variation to avoid repetitive card layouts, so that the page is beautiful. I\'m ready to begin the redesign!\n\n\n**Developing the Hero Section**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the hero section\'s layout, aiming for a distinctive asymmetric design. The new two-column grid prioritizes visual impact and editorial feel. I\'m focusing on the left column with a \"SYS: COMPATIBLE\" tag and impactful headlines in Playfair Display and Amiri. The description will complement the main headlines, and I\'m keen on integrating the search form elegantly within this column. The right column will hold an exciting visual element.\n\n\n**Constructing the Audit Deck**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into creating the interactive \"AccoNet Ledger & Task Engine Audit Deck\" widget, aiming for a high-fidelity look, similar to those found in Stripe or Linear. I plan to build it using React state and ticking elements to simulate ledger entries and live actions. I envision a title bar, status indicators like compliance checks, and interactive rows that display results on click. I\'m focusing on making it a compelling, dynamic product preview. I\'m also planning to review `src/components/Navbar.tsx` to ensure it is premium and tactile, to avoid generic looks.\n\n\n**Refining UI Components**\n\nI\'m now laser-focused on refining UI elements. The `Navbar` in `/src/components/Navbar.tsx` needs a premium feel, achieved by crisp borders, sharp corners and gorgeous display typography. Specifically, the language select picker must be discrete. Auth links need simple, editorial underlines. Meanwhile, I\'m checking `src/pages/Tools.tsx` for elegance with a dynamic tools list and interactive simulation window. The linter\'s running, and the build is succeeding, so I am ready to iterate on the style. I\'m checking the page structure to rewrite `src/pages/Landing.tsx`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Landing.tsx**\n\nI\'m now diving into `Landing.tsx` to preserve existing search functionality related to keywords, wilayas, and specialties, along with their associated state variables. I\'ve confirmed filter passing via URL query parameters, aligning perfectly with `Search.tsx`. The testimonials list will be retained. I\'m focusing on lines 53-368 for a comprehensive redesign, and planning a new hero section with a grid layout.\n\n\n**Crafting the Hero Section**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the hero section\'s design, concentrating on a two-column grid layout for visual impact. I\'m prioritizing typography with a serif-sans-serif pairing. The first column will feature a \"SCF COMPATIBLE\" badge and brand heading, rendered beautifully in Arabic with a serif font. There is an interactive search bar with sharp borders, and some quick links. The second column will display a live-preview mock dashboard, with local credentials check, and dynamic audit checklist.\n\n\n**Refining Page Structure**\n\nI\'m now sketching out the content blocks in `Landing.tsx`. The \"How It Works\" section will be either an alternating layout or a horizontal timeline, styled with crisp serif cards and offset step numbers. I\'m aiming for an authentic, human-designed look. The Featured Specialists section is moving from a grid to an asymmetric, editorial grouping, with a large left column describing the elite partners, and a refined right column displaying their cards.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now completely redesign `src/pages/Landing.tsx` with a premium asymmetrically balanced editorial layout. The hero section is transformed from a standard centered block into a sophisticated split-screen composition:\n- One side houses the high-contrast display typography, the localized subheadings (blending premium English Serif with gorgeous Arabic Amiri and Cairo typefaces), and a compact, sharp search bar.\n- The other side introduces an interactive \"AccoNet Ledger & Task Engine Audit Deck\" widget that simulates compliance checking, validation states, and tax deadlines under the 2026 Algerian Financial System (SCF).\nWe will overwrite the file to perform a complete, clean restructuring."
    thinking_duration {
