  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Registration Logic**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `Register.tsx` component, appreciating its structure. My focus has shifted to the urgent requirement: \"UPGRADE 1 \342\200\224 REGISTRATION WITH DOCUMENT UPLOAD (CRITICAL \342\200\224 ALGERIAN MARKET).\" I\'m outlining a 4-step registration process tailored for \"Professional\" users (Mhni / Professionnel / \330\247\331\204\331\205\331\207\331\206\331\212)\n\n\n**Designing Registration UI**\n\nI\'m now detailing the user interface for the registration wizard. On desktop, I envision a persistent left-side stepper; on mobile, a top progress bar is more fitting. I\'m fleshing out the four steps, focusing on field validations, especially for the Algerian market. Step 1 will cover account info with +213 phone format and a Wilaya selector using coded order. The second step involves professional identity specifics, with carefully chosen specialty options and validation of registration numbers.\n\n\n**Defining Business Registration Steps**\n\nI\'m now diving into the \"For Business\" user registration flow. It will be a 3-step wizard. Step one encompasses account information, including a responsible person\'s details and required credentials. Step two will focus on the business\'s identity, demanding details like the D\303\251nomination sociale, RC number, and NIF. The final step is for file uploads, specifically tailored to business type, allowing for tailored submission with a generated ID upon completion.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now rebuild `/src/pages/Register.tsx` into a highly interactive, double-path wizard for the Algerian market. It features a left-side stepper on desktop for professionals (4 steps) and a dedicated 3-step process for businesses (Mou\'assassa) with advanced custom styling, proper phone number decorators, and reactive fields like startup label certificates and association reciprocity receipts. It integrates the `DocumentUpload` component dynamically, performs form validations, simulates state changes, and triggers successful \"ACC-PRO-[year]-[random]\" reference numbers. Let\'s write the complete code."
