    thinking: "**Localizing the Landing Page**\n\nI\'ve successfully merged the dictionary entries! My focus has shifted to localizing `/src/pages/Landing.tsx`. I\'m verifying the necessary content for translation within lines 120-251 of that file, having already previewed it. Now I\'ll proceed with the translation implementation.\n\n\n**Reviewing Content for Translation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on lines 125-136. Specifically, I need to ensure that the Arabic text \"\331\205\331\206\330\265\330\251 \330\247\331\204\331\205\330\255\330\247\330\263\330\250\330\251 \330\247\331\204\330\261\331\202\331\205\331\212\330\251 \330\247\331\204\330\243\331\210\331\204\331\211 \342\200\242 AccoNet\" and accompanying heading and paragraph are ready for localization. I\'ll need to confirm that this content is correctly formatted for translation and integrates seamlessly with the rest of the landing page\'s design.\n\n\n**Confirming Existing Translation Entries**\n\nI\'ve determined I can use `t(\'heroTitle\')` and `t(\'heroSubtitle\')` directly. I had a small moment of doubt, wondering if the entries existed, but thankfully they do! The existing content is beautifully formatted. Now, I will look through the code to use the translated entries.\n\n\n**Leveraging Dynamic Translations**\n\nI am thrilled! Utilizing `t(\'heroTitle\')` and `t(\'heroSubtitle\')` is brilliant. This approach avoids hardcoded Arabic and ensures dynamic content. In `Landing.tsx`, I\'ve verified the translation integration for lines 140-170, and it\'s perfect; it smoothly transitions from existing translated content. This ensures no hardcoded Arabic and maximum flexibility.\n\n\n**Analyzing French Button and Stats**\n\nI\'m now diving into the French elements on the page. Specifically, I\'m examining a button labeled \"Je suis professionnel\" and the three trust stats: \"248 Experts Agr\303\251\303\251s,\" \"48 Wilayas d\'Alg\303\251rie,\" and \"1,200 Entreprises Actives.\" I need to determine the best approach for localizing this button and these numbers, considering their potential dynamic nature.\n\n\n**Implementing New Translations**\n\nI\'ve replaced the hardcoded phrases! I\'m thrilled with the progress; the button texts \"Trouver un expert\" and \"Je suis professionnel\" are now dynamically linked with `t(\'findProButton\')` and `t(\'joinAsProButton\')` respectively. Furthermore, I\'ve integrated dynamic translations for the trust stats, using `t(\'statPros\')`, `t(\'statWilayas\')`, and `t(\'statBusinesses\')`, which neatly resolve their corresponding text across languages.\n\n\n**Refining Consultant Card Translations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the \"Sofiane Benamara\" card within the hero section, aiming for full dynamic translation. I\'ve decided to use `t(\'heroConsultantCard\')` for the \"Active Consultant Card\" text. For the title, I\'m leaning toward using `tSpec(\'certified-accountant\')`, as it provides a clean translation and already exists. I\'ll integrate `t(\'fieldWilaya\')` for the location information, opting for a simplified format to maintain conciseness.\n\n\n**Implementing Consultant Card Phrases**\n\nI\'m now methodically translating the remaining consultant card text! I\'ve decided to translate the specific remaining fields within the consultant card, and am using a series of translation keys. I am replacing the hardcoded phrases such as \"EVALUATION,\" \"SENIORITE,\" \"12 ans d\'exp.\", \"Disponible imm\303\251diatement\", \"45 000 DA/mois\", \"Contacter l\'expert\" and the three badges with their corresponding translation keys. For example, `{t(\'rating\')}` will replace \"EVALUATION\" and `{t(\'contactTheExpert\')}` will replace \"Contacter l\'expert\". I will make the translation keys `t(\'verifiedOnec\')`, `t(\'certifiedDocs\')` and `t(\'securedContract\')`.\n\n\n**Implementing Statistical Section**\n\nI\'m now concentrating on the statistical section and asymmetric search terminal block, making strong progress! I\'m replacing the hardcoded phrases: \"48 Wilayas\" and \"Du Nord au grand Sud alg\303\251rien\" are now translated. Moreover, \"Tableaux Nationaux\", \"V\303\251rification automatique obligatoire\", \"R\303\251glementation Officielle\", \"Syst\303\250me Comptable Financier respect\303\251\", \"D\303\251p\303\264t s\303\251curis\303\251\", and \"Dossiers d\'agr\303\251ment int\303\250gres crypt\303\251s\" will be translated, making them dynamic. I\'ll translate the asymmetric search terminal block, including the heading, placeholder, all wilayas label, and search button text.\n\n\n**Translating Key Phrases**\n\nI\'m now integrating several crucial translations related to featured professionals, testimonials, and the sandbox section. I\'ve successfully implemented `t(\'featuredProsHeading\')`, `t(\'featuredProsSub\')`, and `t(\'feedbackLocalEntities\')`, enhancing the overall flow. I also used keys for `t(\'testimonialsEditoHeading\')`, `t(\'testimonialsEditoSub\')`, and `t(\'verifiedContractLabel\')`. I\'m also including `t(\'sandboxHeading\')`, and `t(\'sandboxMainHeading\')`.\n\n\n"
