assName` attributes of multiple inputs to provide a more consistent visual hierarchy, and more polished look. I\'ve also just noticed a button in the same section, and I am updating that too!\n\n\n**Refining Input Fields**\n\nI\'m now revising the input field for monthly sales, around line 235 in `src/pages/Tools.tsx`, and changed the styling to be rounded. I updated `className` to include `rounded-xl`, which I\'ve also just applied to the staff payroll input. I am checking the current style of the other fields too, to ensure consistency.\n\n\n**Standardizing Input Styles**\n\nI\'m now striving for uniform input aesthetics. I\'m focusing on consistency for all text inputs. I\'ve updated styles around lines 288-316 in `src/pages/Tools.tsx`. I noticed inconsistencies, and I\'m updating input components to use a full border, rounded corners, padding, and text styling for a more cohesive design.\n\n\n**Adjusting Input Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now changing the input styles in the Tools view for a better look. I\'ve switched input styling around line 301 in `src/pages/Tools.tsx`. Specifically, I have updated the input field for \'Tool 5\' to utilize `rounded-xl`, for better uniformity. I\'m working on the design to make it look sharp. I\'m moving on to improving other inputs in the same view.\n\n\n**Optimizing Button Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating aesthetic changes to the simulation trigger button and outputs. I\'m adjusting around lines 321-349 in `src/pages/Tools.tsx` to provide a consistent visual style, and integrate visual polish with the rest of the inputs. I\'m focusing on consistency.\n\n\n\n"
