  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Visuals**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving in and starting with `src/index.css`. I\'m setting the primary background to `#0B1020` and the secondary surfaces to `#12182B` and `#151C31`. I\'m laying the groundwork for the color palette before moving on.\n\n\n**Mapping the Design**\n\nI\'m now mapping the design system colors to CSS variables in `src/index.css`. I\'ve defined variables like `--color-brand-primary` to `#14B8A6`, `--color-brand-dark` to `#0D9488`, and so on. This should allow for a consistent and accessible premium style across the project. I\'m thinking this approach will make it really easy to implement glass dark card styling.\n\n\n**Refining the Palette**\n\nI\'m now adding secondary and tertiary neutral colors to the design, keeping it dark mode centric. I\'ve also selected some font families: Cairo, Inter, Amiri, and Playfair, with Cairo standing out as a modern option for Arabic text. Now, I\'m rewriting the `@theme` in `src/index.css` to incorporate the premium dark theme, neon teals, and glass utilities. I\'ve considered how theme variables are defined in Tailwind v4 and will make use of them.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will edit `src/index.css` to implement the new dark-fintech color palette, premium glass utilities, and typography defaults so that the entire app converts to a dark mode layout."
